        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-01-03T23:40:34.775Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612\" title=\"Screenshot_20230103-172616\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612_2_225x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20230103-172616\" data-base62-sha1=\"1dzXC0jc5ruwSaPozwd3iE7SOv8\" width=\"225\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612_2_225x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612_2_337x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612_2_450x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/088b2819dd1ceb882e417c3564f3f9d89959b612_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20230103-172616</span><span class=\"informations\">720×1600 122 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Very rare case of a Spite game that was almost fun, though it still suffers from the “ignore all victims completely” problem. Normally I don’t even try to punch through Spite’s healing, but with him having only one Drug for a long time, and playing some extremely powerful and aggressive heroes, I managed to outrace him.  He didn’t start to bounce back until getting a big Drug Raid which let him heal for like 20, but the beatdown continued even after Powers started to fuel his lifetapping.  I would have won before he could flip, except that Skyscraper picked the wrong card for her deathblow… Catch A Ride and probably several other cards would have done it, but instead I picked a Compulsion Canister, not realizing that Rebounding Debilitator would prevent it. And then I was stuck in Huge without any Environment card to throw at him, so he survived an unhelpful Endling play, flipped, and did a fistful of extra damage before being utterly pasted by Idealist.  Thus did I miss my chance to see whether Spite has a different loss screen if you beat him pre-flip, the way Kaargra and Dreamer and Baron Blade all have unique pictures depending on how they defeat you.</p>",
